/*
  core/stressors/security_anxiety.spthy -- f_U for SecurityAnxiety, CEREMONY-AGNOSTIC.
  (The Fearful trigger from the machinery §5 f_M graph; unnumbered in the §4 sigma-catalogue.)

  Migrated to the agnostic interface (AGNOSTIC_STRESSOR_INTERFACE.md). A presence detector (like
  sigma1/sigma3/sigma6 it is a lexicon lookup, not a count), so it reads:

    * !Step(P, sid, action)            -- Layer 1: an OBJECTIVE interaction step (no task name)
    * !Demands(action,'Arousal','hi')  -- Layer 2: the usability verdict, from core/lexicon_tlx

  instead of the old !AuthReq(P,aid) match. An 'authorize' step (granting a sensitive operation) is
  marked high-Arousal by the lexicon, so this fires with no !AuthReq token in the rule.

  Yerkes-Dodson (1908): past the peak of the arousal-performance curve the user freezes / refuses. At
  onset it emits SetMask(P,'Fearful') -- everything below SetMask is UNCHANGED. !StressEnable(P) gates
  per party (Stage B); OnceSecurityAnxiety bounds the onset per party.
*/

rule Trigger_SecurityAnxiety:
    [ !Step(P, sid, action),
      !Demands(action, 'Arousal', 'hi'),
      !StressEnable(P) ]
  --[ SecurityAnxiety(P), SetMask(P,'Fearful') ]->
    [ ]

restriction OnceSecurityAnxiety:
  "All p #i #j. SecurityAnxiety(p)@i & SecurityAnxiety(p)@j ==> #i = #j"
